UPSTREAM SOURCES

  Private Rent Report (quarterly, March 2013 to June 2026), South Australian Housing Trust, from the Rental Bond Data
  Set of the Tenancies Branch, Office of Consumer and Business Services. Data.SA, licensed under Creative Commons
  Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0), https://data.sa.gov.au/data/dataset/private-rent-report
    Changes: each report's suburb sheet read into one table (quarter, suburb, flats and units, houses and all
    dwellings: bonds lodged and median weekly rent); the December 2014 report, which covers July to December 2014,
    left out; the suburb names matched to ABS Suburbs and Localities; Greater Adelaide only in the derived tables;
    one-off batches left out; typical rents of 12-month windows worked out as the middle of four quarterly medians.

  Australian Bureau of Statistics, Australian Statistical Geography Standard (ASGS) Edition 3: Suburbs and Localities,
  Statistical Areas Level 2 and Greater Capital City Statistical Areas, 2021. Based on ABS data, licensed under
  CC BY 4.0. Simplified and converted by Plotlay.
  Australian Bureau of Statistics, 2021 Census of Population and Housing, General Community Profile (persons and
  dwellings by suburb). Based on ABS data, CC BY 4.0. ABS data used with permission from the Australian Bureau of
  Statistics (www.abs.gov.au).

  Base map in the Plotlay project and the app screenshots: Plotlay Quiet, made from OpenStreetMap data
